  "decisions": [
    {
      "prerequisiteGoalId": "22133f29-ef02-4408-8f8d-2bbea3275d91",
      "directDependentGoalId": "642d5ea5-b62f-50c8-b0bd-cf132619725f",
      "verdict": "reject",
      "judgment": "Reject necessity of the full oxidation-number-specific prerequisite as a universal prior mastery barrier. Redox half-equation and atom/charge conservation competence is genuinely necessary.",
      "concreteCounterexample": "A learner can derive Zn -> Zn2+ + 2e- and Fe -> Fe2+ + 2e- directly from the supplied/known species charges, balance O2 + 2H2O + 4e- -> 4OH- by atom and charge conservation, and use 2H+ + 2e- -> H2 in the oxygen-poor acidic transfer. The learner then reasons correctly about both metallic/electrolytic paths, sacrificial versus barrier action, zinc/tin scratches and area effects, differential aeration, unknown kinetics, a testable maintenance plan, and negative steel polarity under impressed current. This route does not require assigning formal oxidation numbers to atoms in polyatomic ions or being able to use the oxidation-number method to derive general aqueous half-equations. That learner can satisfy every current corrosion demand while lacking the explicitly required oxidation-number component of 22133f29.",
      "whyNotAnIncidentalExampleObjection": "The objection is not that MnO4-/Fe2+ differs from corrosion or that a neutral oxygen equation differs from the acidic example. It is the explicit method competence: formal oxidation-number assignment and use is part of the prerequisite goal and is assessed in both current cases, whereas all current dependent equations admit direct atom/charge balancing. That is a genuine method-neutral alternative, not merely a change of substance labels.",
      "necessarySharedCore": "Balanced anodic/cathodic equations, consistent electron exchange and atom/charge conservation are indispensable for dependent e1 and the acidic transfer. Their necessity does not establish the necessity of the entire named method-specific goal.",
      "scopeAndAssumptions": [
        "No weakening of dependent half-equation demands. Correct equations must be independently produced and chemically explained, not copied from a key.",
        "Other actual prerequisites, including galvanic-cell understanding, are available; this review does not certify or alter them.",
        "If a future dependent explicitly requires oxidation-number derivation, reconsider that changed demand; no such requirement is present now."
      ],
      "missingOperativeMaterials": []
    },
    {
      "prerequisiteGoalId": "5b1bb5d9-07b1-5ba9-b320-cc97be917c60",
      "directDependentGoalId": "3eb2a06c-d283-57aa-9eb4-088940c4801a",
      "verdict": "approve",
      "judgment": "Approve the canonical source-information competence as genuine prior competence on the supplied-source route. Do not infer a universal pharmaceutical own-research prerequisite.",
      "concreteNecessityReason": "Full process-chain performance is an application of independently selecting, scientifically structuring and contextually interpreting source information. In A1/A3/A4 the learner must separate a cell-free model signal, a completed characterised batch, an untested scale-up plan and an advertising claim, select which evidence answers which question, and build a connected bounded account. In B2/B3 the learner must use the equal 100mmol basis, distinguish immediate composition from shelf-life, interpret an unrepresentative design survey, and write an appropriate limited internal product statement. New impurity and storage information must change the relevant parts of the argument without changing the meaning of earlier evidence. Removing this source-processing competence leaves disconnected data copying, unsupported claims or an ungrounded station list, none of which meets the four full expectations.",
      "transferableCore": "The cleaning and packaging cases test the same operations: select relevant text/table/process information, preserve reference conditions, distinguish observed/model data from advertising, make evidence origin and limits visible, and adapt a structured explanation to its use. Calcium carbonate, container weights, younger classes and caretakers are example contexts rather than prerequisites of pharmaceutical development.",
      "fullScopeBoundary": "The prerequisite canonical wording is given OR independently researched material. Its own-research AND duty is explicitly conditioned on the BY C9 NTG route. The SH dependent supplies all necessary data and expressly requires no external search; this is a legitimate given-source realization of the full canonical competence. Source indication here means keeping the supplied test/process/survey/advertising evidence origins visible in the argument; the dependent does not add a bibliography or a new research action.",
      "counterexampleConsidered": "Completing the dossier without web searching does not refute the edge because own search is not universal in the prerequisite. Merely knowing generic drug-development stages or calculating 75%, 100/60 packs or 66.7% does not satisfy the full dependent: the chemically bounded evidence interpretation and fresh feedback remain required.",
      "scopeAndAssumptions": [
        "Approval concerns the stable canonical given-source competence, not every jurisdiction-specific extension simultaneously.",
        "No claim that the SH optional theme is universal official duty, that external sources were newly validated, or that practical manufacture or actual marketing occurred."
      ],
      "missingOperativeMaterials": []
    },
    {
      "prerequisiteGoalId": "e0d05c36-eaac-4c75-8ead-3fd5bdafefca",
      "directDependentGoalId": "e675fa94-6e23-59c0-b376-4340bf44c00e",
      "verdict": "approve",
      "judgment": "Approve invariant pure-compound mass-composition reasoning as genuine prior competence; oxide/sulfide cases are transferable demonstrations of this core.",
      "concreteNecessityReason": "The dependent must interpret elemental masses as a composition ratio of a specified pure compound, not as an arbitrary total amount or a starting-mixture ratio. In the water case, a 2:16 elemental mass ratio and a 2:1 atom ratio jointly determine Ar(O)=16 on the given H reference. In A/B, dividing 12:16 and 12:32 by the relative atomic masses yields distinct stable atom ratios 1:1 and 1:2; extra molecular-mass evidence then selects CO and CO2 rather than an arbitrary multiple. Those conclusions represent a compound only because its constituent mass ratio is independent of sample amount. Treating changed scale or excess feed as changed pure-product composition would destroy the basis of formula inference. The prerequisite explicitly establishes exactly this distinction.",
      "transferableCore": "CuO normalisation and the FeS excess case operationalise invariant composition and separation of actually incorporated mass from unreacted feed. Their particular metals, sulfide/oxide labels and numbers need not reappear in the gas tasks. The distinction is semantic rather than merely a familiar ratio calculation.",
      "wholeDependentCoverage": "The added pure oxygen gas E uses density and atomic mass to infer O2 and by itself does not need a binary-compound mass ratio. It does not remove the water and binary-gas expectations: full dependent performance still requires them. Likewise, the fixed-composition prerequisite does not supply equal-T/p assumptions, Avogadro reasoning, relative-mass reference conventions or empirical-versus-molecular discrimination; those remain additional dependent work.",
      "counterexampleConsidered": "Solving only the oxygen/helium density subtask is incomplete. Correctly applying m/Ar mechanically to the two given C/O rows without understanding what constituent ratios mean is not full formula-determination understanding. Absence of an explicit excess-feed row in the dependent is not a counterexample: the excess variation in the prerequisite probes the same product-versus-feed distinction, not a separate necessary knowledge of iron sulfide chemistry.",
      "scopeAndAssumptions": [
        "Numerical values are supplied rounded school-model data.",
        "No claim that constant proportions alone determines molecular size or proves ideal-gas assumptions.",
        "No actual experiment or learner mastery was supplied."
      ],
      "missingOperativeMaterials": []
    }
  ],
